            </note>
            <note corresp="#d131-f3" n="3" xml:id="d131-f3-content">
                <p>Not found.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d131-f4" n="4" xml:id="d131-f4-content">
                <p>Telegram 5552 from Leopoldville to CIA, December
                    24, reported that [<hi rendition="#italic">text not declassified</hi>] Kasavubu had finally signed the decree
                    recessing parliament, but that they had no further information as to when the
                    decree would be implemented. [<hi rendition="#italic">text not
                    declassified</hi>] said Minister of Defense Anany wanted parliamentary approval for creation of a Moyen
                    Congo province first. The Station warned that since parliament was not scheduled
                    to meet again until January 2, this gave more than a week for news of the decree
                    to leak and for the opposition to take appropriate action to block it. (Central
                    Intelligence Agency Files, Job 78–00435R, DDO/ISS Files, Box 1, Folder 12, [<hi
                        rendition="#italic">cryptonym not declassified</hi>] Operations)</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
